LATION</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-11006102-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>11006102</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="XP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-3058605-B2" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>3058605</doc-number><kind>B2</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-4138405-U" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>4138405</doc-number><kind>U</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9057096-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9057096</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9249824-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9249824</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9268509-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9268509</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1020564A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA SANGYO KAISHA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGA HIROMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NONOYAMA NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA SANGYO KAISHA, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGA, HIROMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NONOYAMA, NOBORU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGA HIROMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NONOYAMA NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGA, HIROMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NONOYAMA, NOBORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of cleaning pollutants in exhaust gas from cars using a photocatalytic reaction of a photocatalyst by coating at least part of a road with a photocatalytic layer such as titanium dioxide. Substances derived from pollutants held on a photocatalytic layer are washed off by rain or sprinkled water. In one embodiment, a road (12) undergo drainage-pavement and rain water passes through an outer layer (18) and flows along the surface of a base layer (16) for draining. The outer layer (18) has numerous small-grain-size aggregates (1802) sticking out of the entire outer surface of a concrete layer (1804). A titanium dioxide layer (20) is formed by thinly spraying over the entire surface of the outer layer (18) a mixture of titanium dioxide, cement, filler and water, and has a water permeability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Procédé servant à purifier de leurs polluants des gaz d'échappement de véhicules automobiles au moyen d'une réaction photocatalytique provoquée par un photocatalyseur et amenée par le revêtement d'au moins une partie de la voie de circulation par une couche catalytique, telle que dioxyde de titane. Les substances provenant des polluants contenus dans la couche photocatalytique sont lessivées par la pluie ou par de l'eau pulvérisée. Dans un mode de réalisation, on réalise le revêtement de la voie de circulation (12) dans le but de la drainer et l'eau de pluie s'écoule à travers une couche extérieure (18), puis le long de la surface d'une couche de base (16) afin d'être drainée. Cette couche extérieure (18) possède de nombreux agglomérats (1802) de dimensions de grain limitées se détachant de la totalité de la surface extérieure d'une couche de béton (1804). On crée une couche (20) de dioxyde de titane par légère pulvérisation au-dessus de la totalité de la surface de la couche extérieure (18) d'un mélange de dioxyde de titane, de ciment, d'une charge et d'eau, cette couche de dioxyde de titane étant perméable à l'eau.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>